{
  "name": "grub",
  "_about": "The cockchafer grub (Melolontha melolontha), 4.5 cm long: a fat soft C, curled on its side, wrinkled cream-white, the swollen hind end grey-blue where the gut shows through; a hard orange-brown head with dark jaws; three pairs of long, hairy, brownish legs behind it; a row of dark spiracle spots along each side. It lives three or four years underground eating roots. Coat: the stag beetle's grub (bigger, the end not blue). Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/insects/soft.py on insectlib.py (one smooth body on a chain of bones that ripples as it crawls).",
